WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.080
Let’s say you’re trying to
find some solid information

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.540
about a serious health
problem that concerns you,

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.240
like high blood pressure,
or diabetes.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.880
Yet, everywhere you look,

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:14.600
someone’s trying to sell you
something like vitamins,

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.840
yoga mats, blenders, drugs.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.480
Well, breathe a
sigh of relief

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.560
because all we bring
you are the facts.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.960
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.280
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.680
Did you know that more than
1.5 billion people worldwide

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.800
suffer from hearing loss?

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.560
But in some cultures,

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.480
people retain their
hearing into old age.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.720
Here’s our first story.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.280
In the United States,
age-related hearing loss affects

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.680
about a quarter of those in their 60s,
more than half of those in their 70s,

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.240
and 80 percent of those in their 80s.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.680
More than 95 percent of centenarians
have been found to have severe hearing loss.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.080
Because of impaired communication,
this may lead to social isolation,

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:57.320
loneliness, and depression.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.760
It may even threaten one’s life

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:02.600
due to an associated increase
in motor vehicle accidents.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.280
What can we do to prevent
age-related hearing loss?

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.280
It’s said to be a natural part
of the aging process,

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.200
but that’s what we used to think
about pathological conditions

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.000
like high blood pressure.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.200
The vast majority of people
eventually develop hypertension,

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.280
just like the vast majority of people
eventually lose their hearing;

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.240
so, it must just be an inevitable consequence
of growing old, right?

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.640
But then it was discovered
that there were rural populations

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.240
living in Africa and Asia
that ate and lived healthier,

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.760
that didn’t experience an inexorable rise
in blood pressure as they aged.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.520
So, it appeared hypertension
was more a lifestyle choice

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:43.400
than an aging effect—and the same
may be true for hearing loss.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:46.200
The Mabaan tribe living
in the Sudanese desert

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.360
was found to retain
their hearing into old age.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.440
Other studies on isolated
native populations

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.480
found that exposure
to modern civilization

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.280
appeared to undercut
their hearing advantages.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:59.040
What is it about our modern world
that appears to be leading

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:01.960
to a loss of hearing
as we grow older?

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:05.240
Age-related hearing loss
is a result of the premature death

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.600
of the sensory hair cells
in our inner ear

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.800
which turn vibrations
to electric signals to the brain.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.960
Once they’re lost they don’t grow back;
so, prevention is critical.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.560
The question is:
What's killing them?

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.680
A study of more than 2,000 twins
found that the heritability

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.080
of age-related hearing impairment
was only 25 percent;

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:29.320
so, most of risk
is due to nongenetic influences.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:33.520
Risk factors include repeated exposure
to loud noises, smoking,

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.800
and ototoxic
(or hearing-damaging) medications.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.440
Noise exposure early in life
appears to render the inner ear

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.280
more vulnerable to aging.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.360
Animal studies suggest
exposure to low level

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:48.960
but constant noise over 60 decibels
may also be harmful.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.880
This has not been demonstrated
in humans,

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.240
but if you use a white noise generator
to sleep

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:56.400
it can’t hurt to check
that it’s under 50.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.960
Medications known to be ototoxic
include aminoglycoside antibiotics

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:05.320
(like streptomycin, amikacin,
neomycin, and kanamycin)

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:09.960
which are among the highest risk
medications for hair cell toxicity.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.600
But NSAIDS, anti-inflammatory drugs
like aspirin, ibuprofen,

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:18.520
and naproxen, and loop diuretics
(for example furosemide sold as Lasix)

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:22.400
have also been linked
to progressive hearing loss.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.480
However, the key to the preservation
of old-age-hearing

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:29.760
of the Mabaan tribe may be their diet.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.000
The reason the Mabaan researchers
concluded that their diet

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.560
likely accounted for their lack
of age-related hearing loss

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:39.080
is because they also appeared
to lack something else:

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:41.360
coronary artery disease.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.360
What kills more of us in the industrialized
world than anything else

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.920
doesn’t appear to touch them at all.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.160
Their blood pressures
are also perfect their whole lives

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:53.800
at about 110 over 70 into their 70s
while we, on average, become hypertensive,

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:57.560
exceeding 130/80, starting in our 40s.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:01.000
And no wonder—their diet
is “almost free of animal protein”

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.680
and centered around whole grains.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.800
So, they suggested, in addition
to the absence of loud noise,

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:08.840
that atherosclerosis clogging
the small blood vessels

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:12.080
feeding their inner ears
may be the underlying cause

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:15.680
of age-related hearing loss
in most of the rest of the world.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:20.360
But you don’t know
until...you put it to the test,

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.360
which I’ll cover next,
after dealing with a supplement

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:27.655
shown to slow
age-related hearing loss.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.920
Healthier diets are associated&nbsp;
with a significantly&nbsp;

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:31.280
lower risk of hearing loss,

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:34.840
and for all three diet quality scoring systems
these researchers used,

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.880
avoidance of meat was most strongly
associated with lower risk.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.200
The Mabaan from my last video,
who preserved their hearing into old age,

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:44.480
ate little meat,
but also weren’t eating sugary junk,

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:48.880
explaining their almost total absence
of dental cavities.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:50.880
A high glycemic diet of refined carbs

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:54.600
is also associated with developing
age-related hearing loss.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.560
If it’s the blood sugar spikes,
that would explain why diabetics

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:00.440
and prediabetics
are also at higher risk.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:04.520
Even among whole grains, sorghum,
which is the center of the Mabaan diet,

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:09.240
has a particularly low glycemic index
due to its resistant starch content,

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:14.560
causing about a 25 percent lower rise
in blood sugar compared to whole wheat.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:17.760
Impaired blood circulation
may also explain how noise

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:19.760
damages the inner ear, as loud noises

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:22.640
cause constriction
of the accompanying blood vessels.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:26.680
This may also help clarify the link
between obesity and hearing loss.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.320
Excess weight may just be a proxy
for unhealthier diets,

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:35.680
but the pro-inflammatory state of obesity
can itself lead to vascular dysfunction.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:38.960
Measures of systemic inflammation
seem to directly correlate

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:43.280
with age-related hearing loss,
as do measures of oxidative stress.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:46.520
In my video on brain inflammation,
I introduced

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:49.480
the antioxidant defense activator Nrf2,

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:54.120
called “guardian of healthspan
and gatekeeper of species longevity.”

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:58.280
Those born with a genetic variant Nrf2
that doesn’t encode as well

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:01.200
are significantly more likely
to develop impaired hearing,

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:05.800
implicating the role of free radicals
in the process of hearing loss.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:09.720
You can look in the back of people’s eyes
and measure the amount of macular pigment—

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.200
the lutein and zeaxanthin antioxidants
concentrated in greens—

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.880
and correlate that with superior hearing.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:21.200
The population data on antioxidant intake
and hearing loss is mixed, though.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:23.440
Take vitamin C for example.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:27.000
Some studies show that higher vitamin C
intake is associated with better hearing,

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.480
but others failed to find
any significant connection.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.960
The only way to tell
if antioxidants help or not—

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:38.000
you know the drill—
is to put them to the test.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.120
Adding antioxidants to the diets of rats

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:43.120
seems to help prevent
age-related rat hearing loss,

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:46.000
but doing the same thing
in mice doesn’t appear to help.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.400
The most exciting preclinical data
may be a study

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.760
in which aged rats randomized
to added blueberries

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:55.040
looked like they had a reversal
in hearing deficits,

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:58.560
in fact ending up better
than the young rats.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:01.360
Wait, I thought hair cells
don’t regenerate?

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:06.320
Our ability to hear doesn’t just have to do
with our ears, but our brain.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:10.560
As we age, our auditory cortex
in the temporal lobe of our brain

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:13.600
loses some of its ability to discriminate
and understand speech

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.680
even in a quiet environment.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:20.520
We don’t just need to sense sounds,
but make sense out of them.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.640
That’s where blueberries
seemed to come in,

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:27.480
reversing the age-related cognitive deficits
in auditory processing.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:30.200
But what about in people?

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:34.080
There are studies lacking control groups that
documented improvements in hearing loss,

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:38.800
giving people antioxidant supplements
like vitamins A, E, C, and alpha-lipoic acid.

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.000
But when properly put to the test
in a randomized double-blind,

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:47.320
placebo-controlled trial of a whole list
of antioxidants, the supplements flopped—

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:50.640
no effect on any of the
measured hearing aspects.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:54.720
Is there any supplement that has been shown
to help with hearing in older adults?

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:59.560
Yes, folic acid,
the supplement form of folate,

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.360
found concentrated
in beans and greens.

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:05.680
Some observational studies
had found that higher levels of folate

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:07.640
in the blood seem
to correlate with better hearing,

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:10.520
but maybe that’s just a marker
of eating a healthier diet in general.

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:14.640
So, Dutch researchers set out
on an ambitious three-year double-blind

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:18.520
placebo-controlled trial randomizing
more than 700 older men and women

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:24.120
to take 800 μg of folic acid a day
or an indistinguishable placebo.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:27.320
Excitingly, those who had been taking
the folic acid

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:31.840
suffered significantly less decline
in hearing at speech frequencies.

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:34.560
The effect size was rather small,
such that one might expect

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:37.840
the proportion of men, for example,
who would be hearing aid candidates

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:41.520
at age 75 might drop
from 33 percent to 22 percent

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:44.080
with folic acid supplementation.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:47.720
Also note the study was done
in the Netherlands, where, at the time,

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:50.880
the food supply was not fortified
with folic acid.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:52.840
In the U.S.,
where folic acid fortification

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:56.160
has been mandated
in refined grain products for decades,

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:59.200
it’s unclear how much additional benefit
supplements might add.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:05.400
Regardless, the healthiest sources are dark
green leafy vegetables and legumes.

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:10.280
(A cup of cooked lentils has 90 percent
of adult daily needs.)

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:11.080
Finally today,

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:13.200
we hear about the
results of a diet

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:17.640
that may slow or even
reverse hearing loss.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:21.440
A 2021 scoping review on the role
of nutrition in the development

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:24.600
and prevention of age-related hearing loss
screened thousands of papers

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:28.080
and concluded that “Diets rich
in saturated fats and cholesterol

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:32.800
have deleterious effects on hearing
that could be prevented by lower consumption.”

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:37.960
The case of the Mabaan I noted
before makes for a compelling story,

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:41.480
but on what exactly
are they basing their conclusion?

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.880
It’s true that in laboratory animals
you can prove it.

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:48.040
Randomize rats to added saturated fat
or chinchillas to added dietary cholesterol,

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:51.280
and scientists can show
atherosclerosis-inducing diets

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:54.320
exacerbate inner ear damage
and hearing loss,

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.360
even without noise exposure.

00:09:56.360 --> 00:10:00.400
But that doesn’t necessarily mean
the same is true in people.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.720
There is cogent epidemiological data.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:06.440
For example, a study of thousands of twins
was able to draw a significant link

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:09.240
between a high cholesterol diet
and hearing impairment.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:12.440
In the Blue Mountains Hearing Study,
which enrolled thousands of older men

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:14.720
and women to study
age-related hearing loss,

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:17.320
dietary cholesterol was the nutrient
component

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.200
most associated with hearing loss.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.680
Those eating about two eggs worth of
cholesterol a day

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.840
had 34 percent greater odds
of hearing loss

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:27.320
compared to those only getting
about a single egg’s worth.

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:29.880
Consistent with a vascular cause,
those on statins,

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:33.360
and particularly those at higher doses,
appeared to be at lower risk.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:35.680
The researchers suggest
that high cholesterol intake

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:39.320
may interfere with the circulation
within the inner ear itself,

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:42.480
or atherosclerotic inflammatory changes
could reduce blood flow

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:45.400
to the tiny arteries
feeding the inner ear.

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:50.760
But how about looking inside the arteries
to see if this is actually true?

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:54.200
The extent and severity
of coronary artery disease in the heart,

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:58.640
as determined by angiogram, was found
to closely correlate to hearing loss.

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:03.400
Since atherosclerosis is a systemic disease
affecting the entire arterial tree,

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:07.080
this has relevance for the arteries
feeding the inner ear.

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:09.320
The same was found for the amount
of atherosclerotic plaque

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:11.640
found in the carotid arteries in the neck.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:15.160
The greater the plaque, the poorer the
hearing, and the more plaque they found,

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:17.120
the greater risk of further
hearing impairment

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:19.800
measured over
the subsequent five years.

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:24.640
Getting closer, but how about the arteries
that directly supply the inner ear?

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:29.280
Early autopsy data suggested sclerotic
changes in the blood vessels of older ears

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:32.440
contribute to inner ear degeneration,
and these days,

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:35.720
direct imaging studies correlate
the degree of hearing loss

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:39.840
with atherosclerotic narrowing
of those inner ear arteries.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:44.520
Now all we need is an interventional trial
to wrap it all up in a bow.

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:47.200
Yes, high-cholesterol
and high saturated fat diets

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.800
have been shown to kill off
those critical inner ear cells

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:52.560
and cause hearing loss in lab animals,

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:55.160
but it’s not like you can lock
hundreds of people up for a few years

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:57.360
and force them to eat
different amounts of saturated fat

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.960
and see what happens to their hearing.

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:06.440
Oh, but you can, and they did:
The Finnish Mental Hospital Study.

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:10.640
In 1960, one of two mental hospitals
near Helsinki had their menus changed

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:13.280
to decrease their intake
of saturated animal fat.

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:17.240
Then, after a few years, the two hospitals
switched their menus over.

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:19.760
It was one of the first
interventional trials of its kind

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.400
suggesting that you could decrease
heart disease deaths

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.800
by decreasing saturated fat intake.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:31.040
Ah, but what happened to their hearing?
It followed the exact same pattern.

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:34.080
As their heart disease got worse,
so did their hearing.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:37.020
And then when the hospitals switched,
the reverse happened.

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:38.840
And not just by a little.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:41.560
Those in their 50s
in the lower saturated fat hospital

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.520
ended up with significantly better hearing

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:47.600
than the group in the control hospital
that was ten years younger.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:51.080
The researchers concluded: "our
audiological studies lead us to conclude

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:56.240
that diet is an important factor
in the prevention of hearing loss.”

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:58.440
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:01.640
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:04.120
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:08.720
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:13.880
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:16.440
go to the Nutrition Facts
Podcast landing page.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.800
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:23.440
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite for each of these topics.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:26.200
My last two books were
“How to Survive a Pandemic”

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:29.000
and my “How Not to Diet Cookbook”.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.040
Get ready this year for the
launch of “How Not to Age”.

